<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Cook returns two weeks after his first visit, on the day of his carotid duplex ultrasound and his consultation with Dr. Abernathy-Mensah. He measured his blood pressure at home twice a day for seven days with the upper-arm cuff from the clinic; the fourteen readings average 154/90. He has had no headache, chest pain, breathlessness, weakness, numbness, speech trouble or loss of vision in either eye. He has cut down on salt and walks each day. He has signed the request for his prison medical records, which have not yet arrived, and has met the social worker once. He feels low at times and ashamed when people recognize his name, but he is sleeping and writing. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home blood pressure</td><td>Fourteen readings over seven days, average 154/90</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>None; no stroke or eye symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Lifestyle</td><td>Less salt; daily walking</td></tr><tr><td>Records</td><td>Prison medical records requested, not yet received</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Low at times; ashamed when recognized; sleeping and writing</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

